      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Referral banner shows daily bonus for limited tier and reserves rows",
        "summary": "The `FreebuffReferralBanner` component in the waiting-room screen now branches on the session's `accessTier`: the LIMITED tier renders a quiet one-line daily free-session bonus (capped at `REFERRAL_CLI_DAILY_SESSION_BONUS_CAP`) with a copy-invite-link button instead of hiding the banner entirely, while the FULL tier keeps its GLM 5.2 card and launch button. The waiting room's `referralBannerRows` height budget now adds an `accessTier === 'limited'` case so the scrollbox shrinks correctly for the new branch, and both branches share the existing `flexShrink: 0` guard to prevent the bordered copy button from overlapping the line above it in height-starved landing columns. In `common/src/types/freebuff-session.ts` the `FreebuffReferralInfo` type makes `weeklySessionsRemaining` and `resetAt` optional (documented as full-tier-only, omitted for the limited daily-bonus variant) and updates the `none` status doc comment to describe both tier-specific reward presentations.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/components/freebuff-referral-banner.tsx`, the `FreebuffReferralBanner` component now gates on `accessTier`: the LIMITED branch renders the daily-session-bonus line and shares the same `flexShrink: 0` defensive layout as the FULL tier. In `cli/src/components/waiting-room-screen.tsx`, `referralBannerRows` now branches on `accessTier === 'limited'` to reserve the correct row budget. In `common/src/types/freebuff-session.ts`, `FreebuffReferralInfo.weeklySessionsRemaining` and `resetAt` change from required to optional, and the `none` status doc comment now mentions the limited-tier daily-bonus variant.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "high",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not show the server-side change that begins emitting `referral` blocks on limited-tier `none` responses, only the client handling of them. A second read of the same diff did not confirm that a migration step is required.",
        "changes": [
          {
            "area": "cli/src/components/freebuff-referral-banner.tsx",
            "what": "Adds a LIMITED tier branch rendering a daily free-session bonus line plus a copy-invite-link button, sharing the existing flexShrink and focus-guard logic.",
            "files": [
              "cli/src/components/freebuff-referral-banner.tsx"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "cli/src/components/waiting-room-screen.tsx",
            "what": "Adds an accessTier === 'limited' case to the referralBannerRows height-reservation math so the picker scrollbox accounts for the new branch.",
            "files": [
              "cli/src/components/waiting-room-screen.tsx"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "common/src/types/freebuff-session.ts",
            "what": "Makes weeklySessionsRemaining and resetAt optional on FreebuffReferralInfo and redocs the none status referral field as tier-dependent.",
            "files": [
              "common/src/types/freebuff-session.ts"
            ]
          }
        ],
